  "title": "Visiting the Graves of the Faithful Believers",
  "data": "Greeting the Inhabitants\nTo salute those buried in the graves, say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ الدِّيَارِ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ اَنْتُمْ لَنَا فَرَطٌ وَ نَحْنُ اِنْ شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ بِكُمْ لَاحِقُوْنَ.\nASSALAAMU A'LAA AHLID DIYAARI MINAL MU'MINEENA WAL MUSLIMEENA ANTUM LANAA FARATUN WA NAHNU IN SHAA-AL LAAHU BIKUM LAAHIQOON.\nPeace be upon the inhabitants of these graves, the faithful believers and Muslims. You have preceded us, and we, Allah willing, shall join you.",
  "tabs": [
    "Entering a Graveyard: Dua\nOn entering a graveyard, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ هٰذِهِ الْاَرْوَاحِ الْفَانِيَةِ وَ الْاَجْسَادِ الْبَالِيَةِ وَ الْعِظَامِ النَّخِرَةِ الَّتِيْ خَرَجَتْ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا وَ هِيَ بِكَ مُؤْمِنَةٌ اَدْخِلْ عَلَيْهِمْ رُوْحًا مِنْكَ وَ سَلَامًا مِنِّيْ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA HAAZIHIL ARWAAHIL FAANIYATI WAL AJSAADIL BAALIYATI WAL 'IZAAMIN NAKHIRATIL LATEE KHARAJAT MINAD DUNYAA WA HIYA BIKA MU'MINATUN ADKHIL A'LAYHIM ROOHAN MINKA WA SALAAMAN MINNEE\nO Allah, O Lord of these extinct souls, rotten bodies, and crumbled bones that left this worldly life bearing faith in You, (please) insert into them rest from You and salutation from me.",
    "Entering a Graveyard: Salam\nAnother form to say on entering a graveyard:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنْ اَهْلِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ يَا اَهْلَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ بِحَقِّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ كَيْفَ وَجَدْتُمْ قَوْلَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ يَا لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ بِحَقِّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اِغْفِرْ لِمَنْ قَالَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَ احْشُرْنَا فِيْ زُمْرَةِ مَنْ قَالَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلِيٌّ وَلِيُّ اللّٰهِ.\nASSALAAMU A'LAA AHLI LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU MIN AHLI LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU YAA AHLA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU BIHAQQI LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU KAYFA WAJADTUM QAWLA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU MIN LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU YAA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU BIHAQQI LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU IGHFIR LIMAN QAALA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU WAHSHURNAA FEE ZUMRATI MAN QAALA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU MUHAMMADUN RASOOLUL LAAHI A'LIYYUN WALIYYUL LAAH.\nPeace be upon the group of “There is no god save Allah” from the group of “There is no god save Allah.” O group of “There is no god save Allah,” in the name of “There is no god save Allah,” how have you found the profession of “There is no god save Allah” from “There is no god save Allah?” O He to Whom “There is no god save Allah” is said, I beseech You in the name of “There is no god save Allah” to forgive any one who professed that “There is no god save Allah” and to include us in the group of those who professed that “There is no god save Allah. Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. ‘Ali is the authority from Allah.”",
    "Passing by a Graveyard\nWhen you pass by a graveyard, stop and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَلِّهِمْ مَا تَوَلَّوْا وَ احْشُرْهُمْ مَعَ مَنْ اَحَبُّوْا.\nALLAAHUMMA WALLIHIM MAA TAWALLAW WAHSHURHUM MA'A MAN AHABBOO.\nO Allah, (please) turn them to that to which they have turned and join them to those whom they have loved.",
    "At the Grave of a Believer\nVisit the graves of the faithful believers, preferably on Thursday, though any other day will do. Turn your face towards the qiblah, put your hand on the grave, and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْحَمْ غُرْبَتَهٗ وَ صِلْ وَحْدَتَهٗ وَ اٰنِسْ وَحْشَتَهٗ وَ اٰمِنْ رَوْعَتَهٗ وَ اَسْكِنْ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ رَحْمَةً يَسْتَغْنِيْ بِهَا عَنْ رَحْمَةِ مَنْ سِوَاكَ وَ اَلْحِقْهُ بِمَنْ كَانَ يَتَوَلَّاهُ\nALLAAHUMMARHAM GHURBATAHOO WA SIL WAHDATAHOO WA AANIS WAHSHATAHOO WA AAMIN RAW'ATAHOO WA ASKIN ILAYHI MIN RAHMATIKA RAHMATAN YASTAGHNEE BIHAA A'N RAHMATI MAN SIWAAKA WA ALHIQHU BIMAN KAANA YATAWALLAAH\nO Allah, (please) have mercy on his strangeness, connect his loneliness, entertain his isolation, secure his horror, attach Your mercy to him; such mercy by which he can do without the mercy of anyone other than You, and join him to those to whom he has adhered.\nThen recite [Surah al-Qadr](A101) seven times.\nYou may also recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), [Surah al-Falaq](A117), [Surah al-Nas](A118) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) three times each along with Surah al-Qadr.",
    "Dua for the Dead\nWhen you visit the dead, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ جَافِ الْاَرْضَ عَنْ جُنُوْبِهِمْ وَ صَاعِدْ اِلَيْكَ اَرْوَاحَهُمْ وَ لَقِّهِمْ مِنْكَ رِضْوَانًا وَ اَسْكِنْ اِلَيْهِمْ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ مَا تَصِلُ بِهٖ وَحْدَتَهُمْ وَ تُوْنِسُ بِهٖ وَحْشَتَهُمْ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ.\nALLAAHUMMA JAAFIL ARZA A'N JUNOOBIHIM WA SAA'ID ILAYKA ARWAAHAHUM WA LAQQIHIM MINKA RIZWAANAN WA ASKIN ILAYHIM MIN RAHMATIKA MAA TASILU BIHEE WAHDATAHUM WA TOONISU BIHEE WAHSHATAHUM INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY-IN QADEER.\nO Allah, (please) prevent the soil from harming their sides, take their souls up to You, increase Your pleasure with them, and make part of Your mercy dwell with them so that You will save them from loneliness and entertain their isolation. Verily, You have power over all things."
